Specification (clean-room)
--------------------------

Clean-room from IEEE 1815-2012 (DNP3), an open standard. The CRC-16 is the
reveng CRC-catalogue "CRC-16/DNP" parameters (poly 0x3D65, init 0x0000,
refin/refout, xorout 0xFFFF), KAT-verified.

Secure Authentication (object group 120, IEEE 1815-2012 §7 / IEC 62351-5),
SAv2 symmetric core, is implemented: AES Key Wrap (byte-exact against RFC 3394
§4 test vectors), the SA MAC-algorithm registry (HMAC-SHA-1/SHA-256 truncated,
AES-GMAC), and the g120 message codecs + challenge-response flow. The
SAv5/SAv6 asymmetric update-key change (g120 v8/v10–v15, RSA/DSA +
certificates) remains out of scope; see `SPEC.md`.

Design references (behavioral/structural only, no source consulted or copied)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  - opendnp3 (**Apache-2.0**) — object-group field shapes, function-code /
    status-enum values.
  - Public DNP3 primers (Triangle MicroWorks and others).

Wire-format cross-check
-----------------------

The g120 variation numbers, field layouts, and MAC-algorithm / key-wrap /
key-status enum values were cross-checked against the Wireshark DNP3 dissector
(`epan/dissectors/packet-dnp.c`, **GPL-2.0**) — read as a wire-format reference
for the DNP3-SA object/variation numbers and field layouts, which are facts of
the IEEE 1815 wire format; no code was copied or adapted.
